                                <h1 id=3D"cmake-guide">CMake Guide</h1>
<p><strong>CMake</strong> is an open-source, cross-platform family of tools=
 designed to build, test and package software. <strong>CMake</strong> is us=
ed to control the software compilation process using simple platform and co=
mpiler independent configuration files, and generates native makefiles and =
workspaces that can be used in the compiler environment of your choice.</p>
<h2 id=3D"requirements">Requirements<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"htt=
ps://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/CMake-Guide.html#requi=
rements" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"fo=
nt: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open your terminal and execute:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh">cmake --version
</code></pre>
<p>If the <strong>CMake</strong> version is lower than <strong>3.1</strong>=
, <strong>please upgrade</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li><p>You should use <strong>out-of-source</strong> builds, this means you=
 need to create a different directory than <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong> to ex=
ecute the <code>cmake</code> command.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"step-by-step">Step by Step<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"htt=
ps://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/CMake-Guide.html#step-=
by-step" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"fo=
nt: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<h3 id=3D"linux">Linux<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.coco=
s2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/CMake-Guide.html#linux" aria-label=
=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorj=
s-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>
<p>To compile <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong> for Linux:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2=
d-x
mkdir linux-build &amp;&amp; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> linux-=
build
cmake ..
make
</code></pre>
<p>Execute <code>make help</code> to see all build targets, <code>make &lt;=
target&gt;</code> build specified target</p>
<h3 id=3D"generate-visual-studio-projects">Generate Visual Studio projects<=
a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/=
en/installation/CMake-Guide.html#generate-visual-studio-projects" aria-labe=
l=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchor=
js-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>
<p>To generate a Visual Studio project to compile <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong=
>:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2=
d-x
mkdir win32-build &amp;&amp; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> win32-=
build
cmake .. -G<span class=3D"hljs-string">"Visual Studio 15 2017"</span> -Tv14=
1
</code></pre>
<p>Execute <code>cmake --build .</code> to compile, or open <strong>Cocos2d=
-x.sln</strong> in Explorer to use the generated project.</p>
<h3 id=3D"generate-macos-project">Generate macOS Project<a class=3D"anchorj=
s-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/CM=
ake-Guide.html#generate-macos-project" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-=
icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.3=
75em;"></a></h3>
<p>To generate an XCode project to compile <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong>:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2=
d-x
mkdir mac-build &amp;&amp; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> mac-buil=
d
cmake .. -GXcode
open Cocos2d-x.xcodeproj
</code></pre>
<h3 id=3D"generate-ios-project">Generate iOS Project<a class=3D"anchorjs-li=
nk " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/CMake-=
Guide.html#generate-ios-project" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=
=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em=
;"></a></h3>
<p>To generate an XCode project to compile <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong>:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2=
d-x
mkdir ios-build &amp;&amp; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> ios-buil=
d
cmake .. -GXcode -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=3DiOS -DCMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT=3Diphoneos
open Cocos2d-x.xcodeproj
</code></pre>
<p>The parameter <code>-DCMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT=3Diphoneos</code> is optional, i=
t generates a build for running on the iOS device. If you want to run in th=
e simulator, please add <code>-DCMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT=3Diphonesimulator</code> =
instead, but remember you can't run a metal-support app in the simulator un=
til Xcode 11 and MacOS 10.15.</p>
<h3 id=3D"android-studio">Android Studio<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D=
"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/CMake-Guide.html#a=
ndroid-studio" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=
=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>
<p>If you want to add cmake build arguments, please add it at <a href=3D"ht=
tps://github.com/cocos2d/cocos2d-x/blob/84be684e3858393a6f3efc50e3f95d4e0ac=
92a20/tests/cpp-empty-test/proj.android/app/build.gradle#L25" target=3D"_bl=
ank">external Native Build</a> block of <strong>app/build.gradle</strong> f=
ile.</p>
<!--## Prebuilt libraries feature

To solve long compilation times of the engine source code one can use prebu=
ilt libraries. Using this feature you only need build engine sources once f=
